+/// `0016:1462-1467` bounds `MAX_SEG_CHUNKS` by the same rule the flat map's
+/// `max_chunkref_bytes × N ≤ V / 2` headroom states, applied "against a `seg:` record" — so a
+/// conforming publication never writes a `seg:` value above `V / 2`, and a maintenance repoint
